{"orgCode":"0890","name":"Secretary of State","agencyCode":"0010","agencyName":"Legislative, Judicial, and Executive","description":"The Secretary of State, a constitutionally established office, is the chief elections officer of the state and is responsible for the administration and enforcement of election laws. The Office also is responsible for administering and enforcing laws pertaining to filing documents associated with corporations, limited liability companies, partnerships, limited partnerships, unincorporated associations and pertaining to filing bonds and perfecting security agreements. In addition, the Office is responsible for commissioning notaries public, enforcing the notary laws, and in conjunction with being the home of the State Archives, administering a state records management program and preserving documents and records having historical significance. The Secretary of State is the filing officer for lobbying and campaign registration and disclosure documents filed under the Political Reform Act. The Secretary of State also operates the Safe at Home program, maintains the Domestic Partners and Advance Health Care Directives registries, provides support functions for the Voting Modernization Board, and is home to the California Museum.\n\nPolicy associated with the administration of the Office is accomplished through the divisions of Elections, Political Reform, Business Programs, Archives, Information Technology, and Management Services.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":177675,"cy":496835,"by":243366},"positions":{"py":644.3,"cy":758,"by":782},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":90,"by":151},"nongovernmental":{"py":379,"cy":616,"by":616}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/0010/0890","kind":"department","name":"Secretary of State","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":177675,"cy":496835,"by":243366},"positions":{"py":644.3,"cy":758,"by":782},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":80077,"cy":378807,"by":126333},"special":{"py":83602,"cy":97806,"by":99997},"federal":{"py":13996,"cy":20222,"by":17036}},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0700","kind":"program","name":"Filings and Registrations","code":"0700","amounts":{"py":86269,"cy":100642,"by":103393},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":3261,"cy":3433,"by":3993},"special":{"py":83008,"cy":97209,"by":99400}},"positions":{"py":255.3,"cy":313.3,"by":332.3},"description":"0700 - FILINGS AND REGISTRATIONS\n\nThe Business Programs Division is comprised of three primary areas: Business Entities, Uniform Commercial Code, and Notary Public and Special Filings.\n\nBusiness Entities examines, files, and maintains formation documents for new California business entities and qualifies out-of-state and international entities to conduct business in California; and also examines, files and maintains changes to the records of domestic or qualified foreign business entities to ensure the business entities are properly formed, merged, converted, amended, and dissolved in compliance with California law. Statements of Information containing key officers and contact information are also processed and maintained for public and governmental use.\n\nUniform Commercial Code files certain financing statements allowing lending institutions to protect their financial interest in personal property and established priority in case of debtor default or bankruptcy. Notices of judgment liens, attachment liens, agricultural liens, and equipment liens are also filed in Uniform Commercial Code, as well as notices of various tax liens submitted by state and federal taxing agencies such as the Franchise Tax Board and the Internal Revenue Service.\n\nNotary Public and Special Filings appoints and commissions qualified notaries public for four- year terms, reviews and approves notary public education courses, and certifies to the authenticity of signatures of notaries public and public officials on documents for use in foreign countries. Special Filings include trademarks and service marks as well as surety bonds that certain business entities are required to file, notices of joint power agreements, city and county charters, and claims for successor-in-interest. This area also has disciplinary functions with regard to notaries public and immigration consultants.\n\nThe Advance Health Care Directive (AHCD) Registry maintains AHCDs, which allow a person to indicate his/her medical treatment preferences if he/she cannot speak or make decisions for him/herself. The AHCD also may designate someone else to make decisions regarding medical treatment. AHCDs and related information can be provided upon request to the registrant's health care provider, public guardian, or legal representative.\n\nThe Domestic Partners Registry registers same-sex couples regardless of the age of the partners, and opposite-sex couples in which one partner is at least 62 years old, as domestic partners in California.\n\nThe Victims of Corporate Fraud Compensation Fund provides limited restitution to victims of corporate fraud who are unable to collect through other means on a judgment against a corporation for corporate fraud.\n\nSafe at Home is the State's confidential address program designed to assist: (1) victims and survivors of domestic violence and human trafficking, sexual assault, stalking, and elder/dependent adult abuse; (2) reproductive health care employees, patients, and volunteers who are in fear for their safety because of their affiliation with a health care facility; (3) public entity employees and contractors who are in fear for their safety because of their work for a public entity; and (4) their household members and minor children. Participants in the Safe at Home program are provided with a post office box to use as a substitute mailing address, thereby allowing them to keep their actual residential address confidential. Once enrolled into the program, Safe at Home provides a mail forwarding service and assists participants who qualify with additional confidential services offered by various state and local agencies.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":86269,"cy":100702,"by":103494}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0700/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":3261,"cy":3433,"by":3993},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":3261,"cy":3433,"by":3993}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":3261,"cy":3433,"by":3993}}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0700/f0228","kind":"fund","name":"Secretary of States Business Fees Fund","code":"0228","amounts":{"py":82802,"cy":95679,"by":96870},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":82802,"cy":95679,"by":96870}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":82802,"cy":95679,"by":96870}}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0700/f3042","kind":"fund","name":"Victims of Corporate Fraud Compensation Fund","code":"3042","amounts":{"py":206,"cy":1530,"by":1530},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":206,"cy":1530,"by":1530}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":206,"cy":1530,"by":1530}}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0700/f3254","kind":"fund","name":"Business Programs Modernization Fund","code":"3254","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":1000},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":1000}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":1000}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0700/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":60,"by":101},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":60,"by":101}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":60,"by":101}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":60,"by":101}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0705","kind":"program","name":"Elections","code":"0705","amounts":{"py":80234,"cy":361859,"by":105078},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":65644,"cy":341040,"by":87445},"special":{"py":594,"cy":597,"by":597},"federal":{"py":13996,"cy":20222,"by":17036}},"positions":{"py":112.3,"cy":117.7,"by":121.7},"description":"0705 - ELECTIONS\n\nThe Secretary of State serves as California's chief elections officer and has broad responsibility to administer and oversee federal and state elections held within California. The Elections Program maintains the official statewide database of registered voters, tracks and certifies ballot measures, certifies candidates for placement on the ballot, and certifies official election results. In addition, the program oversees the certification and modernization of voting equipment and the enhancement of election processes. The program works to increase accessibility to voters, provides resources to educate voters on the electoral system, and investigates election related criminal violations as provided by the California Elections Code.\n\nThis program includes the campaign and lobbying registration and disclosure provisions of the Political Reform Act of 1974. Under this law, the Office registers all levels of campaign committees, and reviews for compliance with statutory requirements all state-level candidate and campaign recipient committees, major donors, slate mailer, political party, and independent expenditure committees. The program registers lobbyists (including placement agents), lobbying firms and lobbyist employers, reviews for compliance with statutory requirements the periodic financial disclosure reports filed by lobbying entities, and publishes a Lobbying Directory on the Internet. This program also supports the electronic filing requirements of the Political Reform Act and posts relevant registration and disclosure information to the Office's web site so the public can track where campaign money is raised and spent and what lobbying activity is occurring in state government. A searchable database of campaign and lobbying financial activity is also provided through the web site.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":79727,"cy":96501,"by":70230},"Local Assistance":{"py":886,"cy":265996,"by":35500}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0705/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":65644,"cy":341040,"by":87445},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":65644,"cy":341040,"by":87445}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":65644,"cy":79018,"by":53445},"Local Assistance":{"py":0,"cy":262022,"by":34000}}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0705/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":13996,"cy":20222,"by":17036},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":13996,"cy":20222,"by":17036}},"extra":{"fundType":"federal","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":13110,"cy":16248,"by":15536},"Local Assistance":{"py":886,"cy":3974,"by":1500}}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0705/f3244","kind":"fund","name":"Political Disclosure, Accountability, Transparency, and Access Fund","code":"3244","amounts":{"py":594,"cy":597,"by":597},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":594,"cy":597,"by":597}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":594,"cy":597,"by":597}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0705/f0942","kind":"fund","name":"Special Deposit Fund","code":"0942","amounts":{"py":379,"cy":616,"by":616},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":379,"cy":616,"by":616}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":379,"cy":616,"by":616}}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0705/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":22,"by":36},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":22,"by":36}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":22,"by":36}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":22,"by":36},"nongovernmental":{"py":379,"cy":616,"by":616}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0710","kind":"program","name":"Archives","code":"0710","amounts":{"py":9751,"cy":15690,"by":16251},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":9751,"cy":15690,"by":16251}},"positions":{"py":30,"cy":41.3,"by":41.3},"description":"0710 - ARCHIVES\n\nThe California State Archives establishes and administers a records management program that applies efficient and economical management methods to the creation, utilization, maintenance, retention, preservation, and disposal of state records and acquires, indexes, preserves, and provides reference access to irreplaceable historic materials from the three branches of state government. The Archives acquires physical and electronic records with legal, administrative, or evidentiary value, or that have historical significance. Materials are transferred to the Archives for permanent preservation.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":9751,"cy":15698,"by":16265}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0710/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":9751,"cy":15690,"by":16251},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":9751,"cy":15690,"by":16251}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":9751,"cy":15690,"by":16251}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0710/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":8,"by":14},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":8,"by":14}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":8,"by":14}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":8,"by":14}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0711","kind":"program","name":"Special Items of Expense","code":"0711","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":17292,"by":17292},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":0,"cy":17292,"by":17292}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"description":"0711 - SPECIAL ITEMS OF EXPENSE\n\nThe Secretary of State is responsible for the effective administration of elections and the preparation and distribution of election-related materials. This program funds the election-related activities of parallel monitoring, printing and mailing of Voter Information Guides, Voter Registration Cards and Voter Notification Cards, and election night reporting. This program also funds the Secretary of State costs associated with a Department of General Services-Office of State Publishing warehouse lease for the storage of paper used for the publication of the Voter Information Guide.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":17292,"by":17292}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0711/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":17292,"by":17292},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":0,"cy":17292,"by":17292}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":17292,"by":17292}}}}]},{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0715","kind":"program","name":"DOJ Legal Services","code":"0715","amounts":{"py":1421,"cy":1352,"by":1352},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1421,"cy":1352,"by":1352}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"description":"0715 - DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE LEGAL SERVICES\n\nThe Department of Justice employs a cost recovery model for charging the Secretary of State for assistance provided for caseload worked on behalf of the Agency. This program funds that cost recovery.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1421,"cy":1352,"by":1352}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0890/0715/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":1421,"cy":1352,"by":1352},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1421,"cy":1352,"by":1352}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1421,"cy":1352,"by":1352}}}}]},{"id":"exp/0010/0890/9900100","kind":"program","name":"Administration","code":"9900100","amounts":{"py":47191,"cy":67552,"by":73564},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":47191,"cy":67552,"by":73564}},"positions":{"py":246.7,"cy":285.7,"by":286.7},"extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":47191,"cy":67552,"by":73564}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0890/